From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hevcdec: log repeated Dolby Vision RPUs and skipped NAL units at verbose

"Multiple Dolby Vision RPUs found in one AU. Skipping previous." was a
warning and "Skipping NAL unit %d" an info message. The second fires for
every enhancement layer NAL unit of a Dolby Vision profile 7 stream, so at
least once per frame, and an application listening at warning or info
level receives a message per frame. Log both at verbose level instead.
Parsing and decoding are unchanged, and the decoder's other messages keep
their levels. Applies to FFmpeg n8.0.1 on top of Vivid's patches 0001 to
0011.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for
FFmpeg. Like the file it modifies, it is free software; you can
redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser
General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation;
either version 2.1 of the License, or (at your option) any later
version (LGPL-2.1-or-later).
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
index 0000000000..0000000000 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
@@ -3666,7 +3666,7 @@
     case HEVC_NAL_UNSPEC62:
         break;
     default:
-        av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_INFO,
+        av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_VERBOSE,
                "Skipping NAL unit %d\n", s->nal_unit_type);
     }
 
@@ -3743,7 +3743,7 @@
         H2645NAL *nal = &s->pkt.nals[s->pkt.nb_nals - 1];
         if (s->rpu_buf) {
             av_buffer_unref(&s->rpu_buf);
-            av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_WARNING, "Multiple Dolby Vision RPUs found in one AU. Skipping previous.\n");
+            av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_VERBOSE, "Multiple Dolby Vision RPUs found in one AU. Skipping previous.\n");
         }
 
         s->rpu_buf = av_buffer_alloc(nal->raw_size - 2);
